# MultiplayFishingGame — Project Conventions

## Tech Stack
Unity 6 (6000.3.10f1), C# 9.0, netstandard2.1, Mirror Networking v96.0.1, URP, New Input System, Cinemachine, TextMeshPro

## Folder → Namespace Mapping
- `Assets/Scripts/Network/` → `MultiplayFishing.Network`
- `Assets/Scripts/Gameplay/` → `MultiplayFishing.Gameplay`
- `Assets/Scripts/Data/` → `MultiplayFishing.Data`
- `Assets/Scripts/Data/Models/` → `MultiplayFishing.Data.Models`
- `Assets/Scripts/UI/` → `MultiplayFishing.UI`
- `Assets/Scripts/Managers/` → `MultiplayFishing.Core`
- `Assets/Scripts/Utilities/` → `MultiplayFishing.Utilities`
- `Editor/` → `MultiplayFishing.Editor`
- `Tests/` → `MultiplayFishing.Tests`

## Code Style
- **Using order**: System.* → UnityEngine.* → Mirror → MultiplayFishing.*
- **Braces**: Allman style (braces on new line), 4-space indentation, no tabs
- **Private fields**: camelCase, NO underscore prefix (`lastSendTime`, not `_lastSendTime`)
- **Serialized fields**: `[SerializeField] private camelCase`
- **Public fields**: PascalCase (except SyncVars which are camelCase)
- **Methods**: PascalCase
- **Parameters**: camelCase

## Mirror Networking Patterns
- **Server-authoritative**: Server owns state, clients receive updates via SyncVar/ClientRpc
- **SyncVar**: `[SyncVar(hook = nameof(OnXChanged))] public type fieldName;` — hook signature `void OnXChanged(Type old, Type new)`
- **Command**: `[Command] public void CmdAction()` — client calls, server executes
- **ClientRpc**: `[ClientRpc] private void RpcAction()` — server calls, all clients execute
- **TargetRpc**: `[TargetRpc] private void TargetAction(NetworkConnection target, ...)` — server calls, one client executes
- **Region organization**: `#region Server` / `#region Client` in NetworkBehaviour

## Error Handling
- Guard clauses with early return: `if (x == null) return;`
- Validate all Command/Rpc parameters on server side
- No try-catch in hot paths
- Logging: `Debug.Log($"[ClassName] message")`

## Forbidden Patterns
- `GameObject.Find()` → use references, singletons, or `FindFirstObjectByType<T>()`
- `Update()` for net sync → use SyncVar, ClientRpc, SyncObject collections
- Modifying `Assets/Mirror/` — Mirror is read-only
- Manual `.meta` editing — Unity manages these
- Legacy Input Manager → use New Input System
- `FindObjectOfType<T>()` → use `FindFirstObjectByType<T>()`
- Try-catch in hot paths → use guard clauses
- Underscore-prefixed private fields
